WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.126
Model weights, visual components, context buffers, image tokens,

00:00:03.126 --> 00:00:05.395
and runtime overhead all consume memory.

00:00:05.395 --> 00:00:11.446
Available VRAM or unified memory often determines which model and quantization can run without heavy offloading.

00:00:11.446 --> 00:00:15.985
System RAM still matters when weights or caches spill beyond accelerator memory.

00:00:15.985 --> 00:00:19.389
NVIDIA GPUs have broad local-inference support across many runtimes.

00:00:19.389 --> 00:00:23.549
AMD support depends more on operating system, backend, and model format.

00:00:23.549 --> 00:00:27.331
Apple Silicon uses unified memory shared by CPU and GPU,

00:00:27.331 --> 00:00:31.870
which can make larger models practical but also means the operating system

00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:34.517
and applications compete for the same pool.

00:00:34.517 --> 00:00:40.569
CPU inference is widely available but may be too slow for larger models or frequent images.

00:00:40.569 --> 00:00:45.107
A GPU or accelerator improves throughput when the runtime supports it correctly.

00:00:45.107 --> 00:00:46.242
Measure actual utilization;

00:00:46.242 --> 00:00:50.402
unsupported operations can fall back to the CPU and change performance.

00:00:50.402 --> 00:00:54.941
Hardware tiers such as 4 to 8 gigabytes, 12 to 16 gigabytes,

00:00:54.941 --> 00:00:59.858
and 24 gigabytes or more are useful planning categories, not permanent model recommendations.

00:00:59.858 --> 00:01:02.883
Smaller tiers favor compact models and lower quantization.

00:01:02.883 --> 00:01:06.287
Larger tiers support more capacity, but still need headroom.

00:01:06.287 --> 00:01:10.069
Larger models can improve some tasks while increasing latency, power,

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:12.339
and failure risk under memory pressure.

00:01:12.339 --> 00:01:16.877
Concurrency and image size can matter more than a single prompt benchmark.

00:01:16.877 --> 00:01:21.038
Shortlist configurations that fit comfortably, then test speed, memory, temperature, power,

00:01:21.038 --> 00:01:22.929
and completion under representative load.

00:01:22.929 --> 00:01:28.980
The right size is the smallest configuration that meets quality and reliability needs with operational headroom.
